<article class="env-lemma" id="00AM">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/00AM">Lemma <span data-tag="00AM">6.33.3</span>.</a> Let $X$ be a topological space. Let $X = \bigcup U_ i$ be an open covering. Let $(\mathcal{F}_ i, \varphi _{ij})$ be a glueing data of sheaves of abelian groups, resp. sheaves of algebraic structures, resp. sheaves of $\mathcal{O}$-modules for some sheaf of rings $\mathcal{O}$ on $X$. Then the construction in the proof of Lemma <a href="/tag/00AL" data-tag="00AL">6.33.2</a> above leads to a sheaf of abelian groups, resp. sheaf of algebraic structures, resp. sheaf of $\mathcal{O}$-modules. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      This is true because in the construction the set of sections $\mathcal{F}(W)$ over an open $W$ is given as the equalizer of the maps 
    <p>
      <div class="equation">
  \[  \xymatrix{ \prod _{i \in I} \mathcal{F}_ i(W \cap U_ i) \ar@<1ex>[r] \ar@<-1ex>[r] &  \prod _{i, j\in I} \mathcal{F}_ i(W \cap U_ i \cap U_ j) }  \]
</div>
    <p>
       And in each of the cases envisioned this equalizer gives an object in the relevant category whose underlying set is the object considered in the cited lemma. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>